target: internal/record/parity_test.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestSaysNoSuchRunReadsBothSignals'
expect: FAIL: TestSaysNoSuchRunReadsBothSignals
why:    dropping the exit-code half is the SECOND wrong version of this guard, restored. The word "unknown" is not unique to a missing run: cmd_convergence prints it to STDOUT with exit 1 as the legitimate verdict for a run that exists with no cycles (runlog.py:583-584), so keying on the word alone turned the `no cycles` fixture into a false "the Python found no run". The two signals live on separate lines so this entry and its sibling cannot be staled by one edit — a caveat the review raised against their first version, which anchored both on the same line.
--- old
	if !ok || ee.ExitCode() != 2 {
--- new
	if !ok || ee.ExitCode() < 0 {
